  "id": "motor-dominance",
  "term": "motor dominance",
  "definition": "Motor dominance is a consistent bias to use one side of the body, limb, or direction of movement more than the other, sometimes called motor handedness. It refers to asymmetry in motor behavior and can occur independently of other left-right asymmetries in the body.",
